<circle cx="180" cy="200" r="3.2" fill="#c25b4a"/>
<text x="170" y="196" font-size="11.5" text-anchor="end" fill="#555f6e">(−5, 16)</text>
<text x="100" y="86" font-size="12" fill="#3574d4">y = (x + 5)² + 16</text>
<text x="180" y="230" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" fill="#555f6e">the completed square never dips below 16</text>
</svg>
<figcaption><strong>Fig P04.2.</strong> The completed square drawn: \(y = (x + 5)^2 + 16\) from \(x = -13\) to \(x = 3\) (57 plotted points) — the vertex (−5, 16) sits on the dashed minimum line \(y = 16\), and the curve climbs to 80 at both ends, (−13, 80) and (3, 80). Every plotted point machine-verified against the formula in this pass's lab.</figcaption>
</figure>
